2026-10-31T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2400) 'the worker zone dispatches and a sidecar computes
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2400  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2400) '- The worker zone is tiny and has no GPU, so it owns and dispatches and does not compute. `zone.elf` in worker mode (zone 1) keeps the job queue, the garment's ownership and the asset index.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2400  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2400) '- The GPU stage runs on a sidecar, a client that has a GPU and the pen's sandbox (this Mac in this rung, the Frame when it is idle), which registers with the worker over a `CH_JOB` stream when it connects.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2400  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2400) '- When no sidecar is attached the worker runs the CPU target of the same Lean-emitted kernels (`kernels/cassie/cpp`, the slangc cpp emits under slang-rt, one source two targets) itself, slower and the same answer within RFD66606-2269's intervals.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2400  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2400) '- RFD66606-2293, where this rule lived before the split.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2400  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2400) '- RFD66606-2269, the CPU oracle's intervals.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2400  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2400) 'The sidecar path
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2400  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2400) 'On `strokes_ready` the worker sends the stroke set to one sidecar. The sidecar's `stages/sidecar_stage.gd` runs `curvenet.elf` on compute-rd, then `asset_store` through `asset.elf`, and streams the `.caibx` and the chunks back on `CH_ASSET`. The worker verifies every chunk against its id (`guest/asset`: `parse_caibx`, the buzhash chunker, `sha512_256`, `decompress_and_verify_chunk`, `assemble_from_caibx`, lifted from `fabric_mmog_asset.cpp` onto std types. HTTP, keychain and ACL dropped), writes them under the server's store, records the index hash in its journal, then `zone_garment_spawn(hash)` and `zone_handoff(eid, 0)`. The ghost carries the index hash. Each client fetches by it and assembles.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2400  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2400) 'Check and controls
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2400  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2400) 'Check: the two-client gate counts the garment's owners every tick and finds exactly one. A garment the sidecar made lies inside the CPU oracle's intervals (RFD66606-2269). The Lean chunk property stores random data up to 1 MiB, verifies every chunk and assembles the input.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2400  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2400) 'Controls: one byte of one chunk flipped with the expectation kept must be caught at the worker. A sidecar kernel built with `-ffp-contract=on` falls outside the interval and is named. The worker with no sidecar makes the garment itself and the gate records both times.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2400  1 LINE
 Text:Written

